#! Two requests in flight, the first cancelled. BOTH must get responses and
#! the ordering is not assumed — the server answers on worker threads, so the
#! survivor can land before or after the cancelled one. The harness correlates
#! by id and holds whatever arrives first, which is exactly what a client must
#! do and what a suite asserting arrival order would get wrong.
#!
#! `documentSymbol` for both, for the reason `cancel-inflight` explains: it is
#! the request that reliably reaches a cancellation checkpoint.
name      cancel/cancel-superseded
profile   minimal
env       WOLF_QUERY_TEST_SLOW_MS 1500

initialize
open      hello.lu
wait      diagnostics hello.lu
send      documentSymbol hello.lu
send      documentSymbol hello.lu
cancel    2
wait      response 2
wait      response 3
shutdown
